{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T15:46:32.467Z","author":"glm-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"af466269c8acb904d2fa3336","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:32.467Z","author":"glm-agent","text":"Root cause diagnosis (worktree at origin/main 089e803): the v2026.10.20 tag, npm 2026.10.20 dist.gitHead and the remote tag all name release commit ee029738 ('Release pm-ops v2026.10.20', authored by github-actions[bot]). That release commit bumped package.json, package-lock.json, manifest.json, index.ts and dist/index.js but did NOT touch CHANGELOG.md: git show v2026.10.20:CHANGELOG.md ends at the 2026.10.15 section - zero sections for 2026.10.20 (and none for 10.16-10.19). git log v2026.10.15..v2026.10.20 -- CHANGELOG.md is empty, so the 2026-10-20 run created its release commit during the changelog generation-drift window (the pending-to-tag drift fixed separately in ops-release-changelog-stability / PR #205, which restored main's changelog afterwards). Current main is healthy: the committed changelog has exactly one section for every one of the 61 release-tag versions, and npm view pm-ops@2026.10.20 dist.gitHead returns the same ee029738. The blocker is therefore NOT current main's changelog but the repair's single note source: repairReleaseCompleteness extracts notes only via git show <release-commit>:CHANGELOG.md, and that immutable commit can never gain a section, so every daily run's --repair refuses forever. Fix plan: keep the release commit's own changelog as the primary note source, and fall back to the audit-time committed changelog (regenerated by changelog:full --all-release-tags and enforced by changelog:check plus a new pre-release section gate) only when the historical commit lacks exactly one section; never read uncommitted working-tree state."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T15:46:32.467Z"}],"before_hash":"e67ae557b35b29b72ea5709cfb62010290214fcc32a8176c73dfae4d5d45b018","after_hash":"7311d931cc3850b8b96fd99887cc9fc7f7a02e6b0fa98142086a8ac6a2a76619","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c9d14da066d9856c4e6729a6353bd06beffd671257a4dbdfc1f7eb4d35e47daa"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T18:16:52.191Z","author":"glm-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"af466269c8acb904d2fa3336","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:16:52.191Z","author":"glm-agent","text":"Revert proof (behavioural revert run in a disposable copy of the package worktree, never the checkout): with releaseNotesFor reverted to the pre-fix single-source read of the release commit's changelog, the two new repair tests fail ('a drift-window release commit without its own section recovers notes from the audit-time committed changelog' and 'a release missing its section in both committed changelogs still refuses before writes'); with the section gate's audit gutted and unwired from release:check, the gate tests fail ('the drift shape fails before a release starts', 'verify audits a checkout's changelog against injected tags' and 'the release gate chain runs the section check before a release starts'). All focused tests pass on the fixed implementation (release-repair.test.ts: 27/27; verify-release-changelog-sections.test.ts: 7/7)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T18:16:52.191Z"}],"before_hash":"7311d931cc3850b8b96fd99887cc9fc7f7a02e6b0fa98142086a8ac6a2a76619","after_hash":"7e24a168d1682198f3e1b2cf99d02e03daf4c480d160fd3f7f8ac04ada75670c","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"31ea0aea8112dfd9409ebbf7155d5f7d73909354776a3bf90efa5198627a80b9"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-27T18:23:16.360Z","author":"glm-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"af466269c8acb904d2fa3336","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:23:16.360Z","author":"glm-agent","text":"Local dry-run of the repair (the script has no dry-run flag, so the GitHub Release write boundary was stubbed; everything before the write ran for real from a scratch script, with npm reads on a clean config): the report-only audit shows exactly one failure ('release tag v2026.10.20 has no corresponding GitHub Release'); the repair run verified npm evidence for pm-ops@2026.10.20 (attested provenance, registry identity and gitHead match the tag commit), verified the published tarball against the release tag tree, verified the committed package identity, and then planned the release notes for v2026.10.20 as 'No tracked changes.' - the exact section from the audit-time committed changelog. The only remaining step was the GitHub Release write, which the daily release job's own --repair will perform on its next run; no tag, npm artifact or GitHub Release was changed here."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-27T18:23:16.360Z"}],"before_hash":"7e24a168d1682198f3e1b2cf99d02e03daf4c480d160fd3f7f8ac04ada75670c","after_hash":"3d87ce104b1849cd6cbe326e85ad6414b9ac5b7c5a4775ec4e6071a7418a7611","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"3654f6d572bede0dcf5c92fc3eac503c9b5804db6ca88f5cfd0866f2934fa835"}
